<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>bitcoin++ · {{if .Event.Tag}}{{.Event.Location}} · {{end}}Event report</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/sponsor-report.css?v=recipient-logo1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/sponsor-report-paper.css?v=20261023-demand"><script src="/static/js/sponsor-report.js?v=recipient-logo1" defer></script></head>
<body data-layout="paper" data-readonly="{{.Preview}}">
{{if .DemoAttendance}}<div class="synthetic-banner">LOCAL DEMO · Attendance and registrations are sample data · Program and YouTube figures are sourced snapshots</div>{{end}}
{{if .Synthetic}}<div class="synthetic-banner">SYNTHETIC DEMO DATA · Layout testing only · Not actual event statistics</div>{{end}}
<nav class="report-tools" aria-label="Report tools"><a href="/admin/reports/annual">Annual reports →</a>{{if .Event.Tag}}<a href="/{{.Event.Tag}}/admin">← Event admin</a>{{else}}<a href="/admin">← Admin</a>{{end}}<form method="get" action="/admin/reports"><label>Event<select name="event" required><option value="">Choose an event</option>{{range .Options}}<option value="{{.Tag}}" {{if eq .Tag $.Event.Tag}}selected{{end}}>{{.Location}} · {{.Title}} · {{.Period}}</option>{{end}}</select></label><button>Open event report</button></form>{{if .Event.Tag}}<label>Format<select id="report-layout"><option value="paper">Paper report · A4 portrait</option><option value="slides">Slides · landscape</option></select></label><button type="button" id="report-edit">Edit report</button><button type="button" id="report-print">Print / Save as PDF</button>{{end}}</nav>
{{if .Message}}<p class="notice" role="status">{{.Message}}</p>{{end}}
{{if not .Event.Tag}}<main class="report-page"><p class="eyebrow">Partner reports / By event</p><h1>One gathering.<br>A story worth sharing.</h1><p>Select an event to prepare its speaker highlights, program recap, hackathon results, and judge portraits.</p><div class="event-list">{{range .Options}}<a href="/admin/reports?event={{.Tag}}"><strong>{{.Location}} · {{.Title}}</strong><span>{{.Period}} →</span></a>{{else}}<p>No published events are available yet.</p>{{end}}</div></main>{{else}}
<details class="report-editor"><summary>Edit narrative & review data sources</summary>{{if .Preview}}<p class="preview-status">Public-source preview: narrative edits can be previewed here, but saving is disabled. No production data is connected.</p>{{end}}<p>Save before printing. Empty counts stay unreported. Select speakers and panels, confirm delivered sessions, and supply comparable views to rank talks.</p>
<aside class="report-data-guide" aria-label="Sources needed to finish this draft"><h2>Finish the numbers</h2>
{{if .Preview}}<p>This preview uses public program and result pages. Open this event’s report in the running admin application to load registration, volunteer, project and payout records.</p>{{end}}
<ul>
<li><strong>Program chart:</strong> check the delivered sessions against recordings or the stage manager’s final running order, then confirm the complete program review below. A published schedule alone does not confirm delivery.</li>
<li><strong>Views chart:</strong> export per-video analytics from YouTube Studio or X, match each recording to its session, and enter one platform’s counts with the same period and export date. A session without a comparable count should stay blank.</li>
<li><strong>Prize chart:</strong> reconcile finalized award results with the event’s payout records. External payments must be recorded and verified before they count; the advertised prize pool is not a payout total.</li>
<li><strong>Attendance and volunteers:</strong> review event check-ins and shift assignments. These measure unique checked-in attendees and assigned volunteers; daily attendance is not collected.</li>
<li><strong>Applications:</strong> use the original CFP intake export, with duplicate and withdrawn submissions handled consistently. Enter the verified count and source below.</li>
<li><strong>Teams and participants:</strong> review submitted projects and their member lists. Finalize award results to populate the winning-project cards.</li>
</ul><p>Before sharing, review the opening note, panel takeaways, judge profiles and closing priorities. This guide stays out of the printed report.</p></aside>
<form method="post" id="report-edit-form"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{.CSRF}}"><input type="hidden" name="revision" value="{{.Revision}}">
<fieldset><legend>Report recipient</legend><label>Prepared for<select id="report-recipient" name="prepared_for_org_id"><option value="">Our partners</option>{{if and (not .SelectedSponsor.ID) (index .Saved "prepared_for")}}<option value="legacy" selected>{{.PreparedFor}} · previous recipient</option>{{end}}{{range .Sponsors}}<option value="{{.ID}}" data-name="{{.Name}}" data-logo="{{.Logo}}" {{if eq .ID $.SelectedSponsor.ID}}selected{{end}}>{{.Name}}</option>{{end}}</select></label><p>Choose an organization from this event’s sponsorships. Its name and logo appear on the cover and acknowledgments. Save before exporting. This updates the current event draft; it does not create a separate draft per sponsor.</p>{{if not .Sponsors}}<p>No sponsors are attached to this event yet. Add a sponsorship in event administration to populate this list.</p>{{end}}</fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Your report, in your words</legend><p>Use **bold**, *italic*, headings, lists and [links](https://example.com). Your opening message and closing text are saved for this event. Preview updates as you type; save when ready.</p><p id="report-save-status" role="status">{{if .Synthetic}}Demo editor — preview only; changes are not saved.{{else}}Draft loaded.{{end}}</p>{{range .Sections}}<section class="narrative-editor"><label for="report-{{.Key}}">{{.Title}}</label><div class="narrative-columns"><div><div class="markdown-toolbar" aria-label="Formatting for {{.Title}}"><button type="button" data-markdown="bold" data-target="report-{{.Key}}">Bold</button><button type="button" data-markdown="italic" data-target="report-{{.Key}}">Italic</button><button type="button" data-markdown="heading" data-target="report-{{.Key}}">Heading</button><button type="button" data-markdown="list" data-target="report-{{.Key}}">List</button><button type="button" data-markdown="link" data-target="report-{{.Key}}">Link</button></div><textarea id="report-{{.Key}}" name="{{.Key}}" data-report-section="{{.Key}}" rows="12" maxlength="12000" aria-describedby="preview-status-{{.Key}}">{{.Text}}</textarea></div><div><p class="preview-label">Live preview</p><div class="markdown-preview report-markdown" id="preview-{{.Key}}">{{.Markdown}}</div><p class="preview-status" id="preview-status-{{.Key}}" role="status">Preview up to date</p></div></div></section>{{end}}<button {{if or .Synthetic .Preview}}disabled{{end}}>Save event draft</button></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Attendance &amp; applications</legend><p>Source records: {{.Registrations}} registrations · {{.Attendees}} unique checked-in attendees. These remain available for review even when not featured in the sponsor edition.</p><p>Unique checked-in attendees are automatic. Daily attendance is not collected.</p><label>Verified talk applications received<input type="number" name="applications" min="0" max="1000000000000" value="{{with .Applications}}{{.}}{{end}}" placeholder="Not supplied"></label><label>Application count note (optional, internal)<input name="applications_source" value="{{index .Saved "applications_source"}}" placeholder="Optional: how you verified this count" maxlength="12000"></label><details><summary>Review proposal status breakdown</summary><dl>{{range .ProposalStatuses}}<div><dt>{{.Label}}</dt><dd>{{.Value}}</dd></div>{{else}}<p>No database breakdown available in this preview.</p>{{end}}</dl><p>Review invitations and organizer-created sessions before entering a verified application count. Multiple proposals from one person are separate applications; this is not a unique-applicant count.</p></details><p>{{.Proposals}} program proposal records exist. These may include invitations and admin-created sessions, so they are not automatically labeled applications.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset id="x-post-attribution"><legend>X post attribution</legend>
<input type="hidden" name="x_posts_editor" value="yes">
<p>Account: @{{.PostLibrary.Account}} · Snapshot: {{.PostLibrary.Collected}} · {{len .PostLibrary.Posts}} posts. Suggestions use links, program titles and event mentions, never dates alone. Only included posts count toward this event. Posts may belong to several events; annual totals deduplicate them.</p>
<button name="action" value="refresh_x_posts" {{if .Preview}}disabled{{end}}>Save draft &amp; refresh X posts</button>
<button name="action" value="approve_x_posts" {{if .Preview}}disabled{{end}}>Include suggested matches &amp; save</button>
<p>{{index .Saved "x_posts_status"}}</p>
<details><summary>Review and assign posts · {{len .ApprovedPosts}} included</summary>
<label>Find a post<input type="search" id="report-post-search" placeholder="Search text, link, or matching reason"></label>
<label>Show<select id="report-post-filter"><option value="all">All posts</option><option value="suggested">Suggested matches</option><option value="included">Included</option><option value="pending">Unreviewed</option></select></label>
<div class="report-post-review-list">{{range .PostReview}}<article class="report-post-review" data-suggested="{{.Suggested}}"><p>{{.Text}}</p><p><a href="{{.URL}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open post ↗</a> · {{.Display}} impressions · {{.Created}}</p><p>{{.Reason}}</p><label>Use in this event report<select name="x_post_{{.ID}}"><option value="" {{if eq .Choice ""}}selected{{end}}>Unreviewed · not counted</option><option value="include" {{if eq .Choice "include"}}selected{{end}}>Include</option><option value="exclude" {{if eq .Choice "exclude"}}selected{{end}}>Exclude from this event</option></select></label></article>{{end}}</div>
</details><p>Unassigned posts remain available for account-wide annual reporting. Excluding a post here does not change another event's assignment. Included post impressions replace the manual X impressions field in the rendered report.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset id="reach-editor"><legend>Beyond the room · event reach</legend><p>Use event-specific video and post exports, not whole-account totals. Record the selected video/post IDs or export filename and how many items are covered. Blank means unknown; enter 0 only when the export reports zero. Save to refresh the report metrics.</p>
{{range .ReachPlatforms}}<section><h3>{{.Name}}</h3><div class="editor-grid">{{range .Metrics}}<label>{{.Label}}<input name="{{.Key}}" value="{{.Value}}" type="number" min="0" max="1000000000000" placeholder="Not supplied"></label>{{end}}<label>Source / account / export reference<input name="reach_{{.Key}}_source" value="{{.Source}}" maxlength="12000"></label><label>Reporting period<input name="reach_{{.Key}}_period" value="{{.Period}}" placeholder="Exact date range or lifetime through date" maxlength="12000"></label><label>Export date<input name="reach_{{.Key}}_date" value="{{.Date}}" type="date"></label><label>Event content included / coverage<input name="reach_{{.Key}}_coverage" value="{{.Coverage}}" placeholder="Selected Nairobi video/post IDs; count included out of total" maxlength="12000"></label></div></section>{{end}}
<p>External-source views are a subset of YouTube views, not an additional audience. Impressions and video views use different definitions; do not add them together or describe them as unique people.</p></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Speaker geography</legend><p>Travel origins load from each speaker’s event form (I’ll be traveling from). Recognized city names are mapped automatically to approximate city centres. Resolve ambiguous responses or add coordinates manually. Coordinates may stay blank while you review. Report corrections do not change the original speaker form. Save to refresh the map.</p><details><summary>Review {{.SpeakerCount}} speaker locations</summary>{{range .SpeakerLocations}}<h3>{{.Name}}</h3><div class="editor-grid"><label>Place<input name="speaker_location_{{.ID}}_place" value="{{.Place}}" maxlength="1000"></label><label>Latitude<input name="speaker_location_{{.ID}}_lat" value="{{.Latitude}}" type="number" step="any" min="-90" max="90"></label><label>Longitude<input name="speaker_location_{{.ID}}_lon" value="{{.Longitude}}" type="number" step="any" min="-180" max="180"></label><label>Confirmation / source<input name="speaker_location_{{.ID}}_source" value="{{.Source}}" maxlength="1000"></label></div>{{end}}</details></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Highlighted speakers</legend><div class="editor-grid">{{range .Speakers}}<label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="speaker_{{.ID}}" value="yes" {{if .Highlight}}checked{{end}}>{{.Name}} · {{.Company}}</label>{{else}}<p>No accepted program speakers found.</p>{{end}}</div></fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Delivered sessions, popular talks &amp; core panels</legend><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="program_reviewed" value="yes" {{if .ProgramReviewed}}checked{{end}}>I have reviewed the delivery checkboxes for the complete program.</label><p>Delivery totals remain blank until reviewed. Only sessions with an end time in the past can be confirmed.</p><div class="editor-grid"><label>Comparable view metric<select name="analytics_metric"><option value="">Choose metric</option><option {{if eq (index .Saved "analytics_metric") "YouTube views"}}selected{{end}}>YouTube views</option><option {{if eq (index .Saved "analytics_metric") "X video views"}}selected{{end}}>X video views</option></select></label><label>Reporting period<input name="analytics_period" value="{{index .Saved "analytics_period"}}" placeholder="Lifetime through date, or exact date range" maxlength="12000"></label><label>Export date<input type="date" name="analytics_date" value="{{index .Saved "analytics_date"}}"></label><label>Analytics source<input name="analytics_source" value="{{index .Saved "analytics_source"}}" placeholder="Channel/account and export reference" maxlength="12000"></label></div>
{{range .Sessions}}<article class="session-editor"><h3>{{.Title}}</h3><p>{{.Kind}} · {{.Speakers}}</p><div class="editor-grid"><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="delivered_{{.ID}}" value="yes" {{if .Delivered}}checked{{end}}>Delivered</label>{{if eq .Kind "panel"}}<label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="panel_{{.ID}}" value="yes" {{if .Core}}checked{{end}}>Feature this panel</label>{{end}}<label>Views<input name="views_{{.ID}}" type="number" min="0" max="1000000000000" value="{{with .Views}}{{.}}{{end}}" placeholder="Not supplied"></label></div><label>Why this session matters<textarea name="session_note_{{.ID}}" rows="2" maxlength="12000">{{.Note}}</textarea></label></article>{{else}}<p>No accepted program sessions found.</p>{{end}}</fieldset>
<fieldset><legend>Judge highlights</legend><p>Portraits and names come from existing profiles. No substitute portraits are generated.</p>{{range .Judges}}<label>{{.Name}} · {{.Role}}<textarea name="judge_note_{{.ID}}" rows="2" maxlength="12000" placeholder="Relevant expertise, contribution, or an approved quote">{{.Note}}</textarea></label>{{else}}<p>No judge assignments found.</p>{{end}}</fieldset><button {{if or .Synthetic .Preview}}disabled{{end}}>Save event draft</button><fieldset><legend>Recording highlights · X + YouTube</legend><p>Sponsor pages lead with platform totals of at least 1,000 views. Individual recordings appear as visual highlights without view counters. Registration headlines start at 100. All source values remain available here.</p><details><summary>Review all recording counts</summary>{{range .Media}}<p>{{.Platform}} · {{.Title}} · {{.Views}} views · {{.CollectionDate}}</p>{{end}}</details><p>Recordings attached to the program are matched automatically. Add full-day broadcasts or other event videos below, one URL per line. For a YouTube moment, append a space and its start time in seconds (for example 135). These are watch links, not newly edited clips.</p><label>Additional event recordings<textarea name="media_links" rows="5" maxlength="12000">{{index .Saved "media_links"}}</textarea></label><button type="submit" name="action" value="refresh_media" {{if .Preview}}disabled{{end}}>Save draft &amp; refresh recording views</button><p>{{index .Saved "media_status"}}</p><p>Public recordings only. Refresh uses connected accounts and may take a minute. Lifetime video views are separate from annual impressions and are never added to manual reach totals.</p></fieldset></form></details>
<main>
{{template "report_paper" .}}
<div class="slide-edition">
<header class="cover report-page"><div class="cover-ticker">• bitcoin++ • event report • open-source builders • technical conversations • hackathons • community •</div><div class="cover-edition"><strong>Event report</strong><span>{{.Event.Location}}</span></div><div class="cover-wordmark">bitcoin++</div><span class="cover-spark" aria-hidden="true">✦</span><div class="cover-bottom"><div><p class="eyebrow">{{.Event.Period}}</p><h1>{{.Event.Title}}</h1>{{template "report_recipient_logo" .}}<p class="partners">Prepared for <span data-report-recipient>{{.PreparedFor}}</span></p></div><p class="cover-tagline">Built together.<br>Developing the frontier of bitcoin.</p></div><p class="draft-mark">{{if .Preview}}LAYOUT DRAFT · Unavailable metrics remain blank.{{else}}WORKING DRAFT · Confirm narrative, program delivery, and source coverage before sharing.{{end}}</p></header>
{{with .Event.LeadImage}}<section class="report-page event-artwork"><img src="{{.}}" alt="Lead artwork for {{$.Event.Title}} in {{$.Event.Location}}"><div class="artwork-caption"><span class="eyebrow">{{$.Event.Period}}</span><h2>{{$.Event.Location}}</h2><p>{{$.Event.Title}} · Event artwork</p></div></section>{{end}}
{{if .Event.VenueImages}}<section class="report-page event-setting"><div class="page-rail"><strong>bitcoin++ event report</strong><span>/ the setting</span><b>{{.Event.Tag}}</b></div><h2>A sense of place.</h2><p class="setting-intro">{{.Event.Location}} · Images from the event website’s venue section.</p><div class="setting-grid">{{range $i,$src := .Event.VenueImages}}<figure><img src="{{$src}}" alt="{{$.Event.Location}} — setting image {{ $i }} from the event website"></figure>{{end}}</div><p class="small">City, landscape and venue imagery selected for this edition.</p></section>{{end}}
<section class="report-page scorecard"><div class="page-rail"><strong>bitcoin++ event report</strong><span>§01 / the event in numbers</span><b>{{.Event.Tag}}</b></div><h2>Who came.<br>What got built.</h2><div class="metric-grid">{{range .HeadlineMetrics}}<article><strong>{{.Value}}</strong><span>{{.Label}}</span><small>{{.Note}}</small></article>{{end}}</div><p class="small">Dashes mean not supplied or not reviewed, not zero.</p></section>
{{range .Sections}}<section class="report-page story" data-section="{{.Key}}"><div class="page-rail"><strong>bitcoin++ event report</strong><span>/ {{.Key}}</span><b>{{$.Event.Tag}}</b></div><h2>{{.Title}}</h2><div class="story-text {{if ne .Key "social"}}report-markdown{{end}}">{{if eq .Key "social"}}{{.Text}}{{else}}{{.Markdown}}{{end}}</div>
{{if eq .Key "program"}}<h3 class="subheading">Highlighted speakers</h3><div class="people-grid">{{$shown := false}}{{range $.Speakers}}{{if .Highlight}}{{$shown = true}}{{template "report_person" .}}{{end}}{{end}}{{if not $shown}}<p class="empty-note">Select speaker highlights from this event’s program in the editor.</p>{{end}}</div>{{end}}
{{if eq .Key "panels"}}<div class="panel-list">{{range $.Panels}}<article><p class="eyebrow">Panel discussion</p><h3>{{.Title}}</h3><p>{{.Speakers}}</p>{{with .Note}}<p class="editorial-note">{{.}}</p>{{end}}{{template "report_recordings" .}}</article>{{else}}<p class="empty-note">Choose this event’s core panel discussions in the editor.</p>{{end}}</div>{{end}}
{{if eq .Key "hackathon"}}<div class="award-summary"><span><b>{{if $.Preview}}—{{else}}{{$.Teams}}{{end}}</b> submitted project teams</span><span><b>{{if $.Preview}}—{{else}}{{$.SatsDisplay}}{{end}}</b> sats recorded as distributed</span></div><h3 class="subheading">The winning projects</h3><div class="winner-grid">{{range $.Winners}}<article class="winner-card">{{if .Image}}<img src="{{.Image}}" alt="{{.Title}} project image">{{end}}<p class="eyebrow">{{.Awards}}</p><h3>{{.Title}}</h3><p>{{.Description}}</p>{{template "report_winner_team" .}}{{with .PrizeFigure}}<p class="report-prize-amount"><strong>{{.Value}}</strong> {{.Label}}</p>{{end}}<div class="report-links">{{if .GitHub}}<a href="{{.GitHub}}">Explore the code ↗</a>{{end}}{{if .Demo}}<a href="{{.Demo}}">Project / demo ↗</a>{{end}}</div></article>{{else}}<p class="empty-note">No finalized winning projects found in the event records. Reconcile historical results before publication.</p>{{end}}</div>{{end}}
{{if eq .Key "judges"}}<div class="people-grid judge-grid">{{range $.Judges}}{{template "report_person" .}}{{else}}<p class="empty-note">Judge highlights will use this event’s assigned judges and profile photos.</p>{{end}}</div>{{end}}
<footer>NYDIG · HRF · Btrust <span>bitcoin++ / {{$.Event.Tag}}</span></footer></section>{{if eq .Key "note"}}{{range $.Charts}}{{$chart := .}}<section class="report-page chart-page" data-chart="{{.Kind}}"><div class="page-rail"><strong>bitcoin++ event report</strong><span>/ {{.Unit}}</span><b>{{$.Event.Tag}}</b></div><h2>{{.Title}}</h2>{{if .Hero}}<div class="chart-takeaway"><strong>{{.Hero}}</strong><span>{{.Caption}}</span></div>{{end}}<p class="chart-note">{{.Note}}</p>{{if .Rows}}<figure class="report-chart">{{if .Donut}}<div class="donut-layout"><svg class="donut-chart" viewBox="0 0 220 220" role="img" aria-label="{{.Title}}: {{.DonutTotal}} {{.Unit}}"><circle cx="110" cy="110" r="78" fill="none" stroke="#ddd" stroke-width="34"/>{{range .Donut}}<circle cx="110" cy="110" r="78" pathLength="100" fill="none" stroke="{{.Color}}" stroke-width="34" stroke-dasharray="{{.Percent}} 100" stroke-dashoffset="{{.Offset}}" transform="rotate(-90 110 110)"><title>{{.Label}}: {{.Value}} ({{printf "%.1f" .Percent}}%)</title></circle>{{end}}<text x="110" y="110" text-anchor="middle" class="donut-total">{{.DonutTotal}}</text><text x="110" y="132" text-anchor="middle" class="donut-unit">{{.Unit}}</text></svg><div class="donut-legend">{{range .Donut}}<div class="donut-key"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6" cy="6" r="5" fill="{{.Color}}" stroke="#000" stroke-width=".5"/></svg><div><span>{{.Label}}</span><strong>{{.Value}} <small>{{printf "%.1f" .Percent}}%</small></strong></div></div>{{end}}</div></div><figcaption>Share of {{.Unit}} · percentages rounded to one decimal place</figcaption>{{else}}<figcaption>{{.Unit}} · shared linear scale from zero</figcaption>{{if eq .Kind "team-sizes"}}<div class="histogram" role="img" aria-label="Project team-size distribution">{{range .Rows}}<div class="histogram-bin"><strong>{{.Value}}</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 50 100" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><rect class="bar-track" width="50" height="100"/><rect class="bar-fill" x="0" y="{{.Y}}" width="50" height="{{.Width}}"/></svg><span>{{.Label}}</span></div>{{end}}</div><p class="small">Members per project → · bar heights show project counts</p>{{else}}{{range .Rows}}<div class="chart-row"><div class="chart-label"><div>{{if .URL}}<a href="{{.URL}}">{{.Label}}</a>{{else}}<span>{{.Label}}</span>{{end}}{{with .Detail}}<small>{{.}}</small>{{end}}</div><strong>{{if eq $chart.Kind "prizes"}}{{.SatsDisplay}}{{else}}{{.Value}}{{end}}</strong></div><svg viewBox="0 0 100 3" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="bar-track" width="100" height="3"/><rect class="bar-fill" width="{{.Width}}" height="3"/></svg></div>{{end}}{{end}}{{end}}</figure>{{else}}<div class="chart-empty"><span>Data pending</span><p>{{.Empty}}</p></div>{{end}}</section>{{end}}
{{end}}{{end}}
<section class="report-page methodology"><div class="page-rail"><strong>bitcoin++ event report</strong><span>/ sources &amp; definitions</span><b>{{.Event.Tag}}</b></div><h2>A clear account<br>of the gathering.</h2><dl><dt>Event and edition</dt><dd>{{.Event.Title}} · {{.Event.Location}} · {{.Event.Period}}. Generated {{.Generated}}. Live records may change; save the PDF to preserve the edition you send.</dd><dt>Attendance</dt><dd>Unique checked-in attendees are deduplicated by person or email. Historical attendance survives account deletion. Daily attendance is not collected.</dd><dt>Program and applications</dt><dd>Talks include keynotes; workshops and panels are separate. Delivered counts require an editor’s complete program review. The proposal table also contains invitations and admin-created sessions, so an independently verified intake count supplies the application metric. Archived and unaccepted sessions are excluded.</dd><dt>People and popularity</dt><dd>Volunteer crew counts unique people assigned to shifts, not confirmed attendance. Highlighted speakers and panels are editorial choices. Popular sessions are ranked only within the imported analytics set using one metric, source, period, and export date. Views do not establish in-room popularity.</dd><dt>Hackathon teams, awards, and payouts</dt><dd>Project teams count submitted/advanced projects; the same team submitting multiple projects may count more than once. Participants are distinct members of those projects. Winning cards require finalized results and non-archived awarded prizes. Sats count distribution records of type sats marked sent or claimed, not announced prizes or independently verified settlement. Sats labels use k for thousands and M for millions, rounded to two decimal places. External, pooled, or historical payouts require reconciliation.</dd><dt>Portraits and evidence</dt><dd>Speaker and judge photos come from existing profiles. Missing photos are marked explicitly. Confirm photo rights, names, affiliations, quotes, and historical data coverage before sending. No private contact or payout details are included.</dd></dl><p class="closing">Thank you for helping the people building Bitcoin find one another.</p></section>
</div></main>{{end}}</body></html>
{{define "report_person"}}<article class="person-card">{{if .Photo}}<img src="{{.Photo}}" alt="Portrait of {{.Name}}">{{else}}<div class="portrait-missing">Portrait not supplied</div>{{end}}<h3>{{.Name}}</h3>{{with .Company}}<p>{{.}}</p>{{end}}{{with .Role}}<p class="eyebrow">{{.}}</p>{{end}}{{with .Note}}<p class="editorial-note">{{.}}</p>{{end}}</article>{{end}}
{{define "report_recordings"}}<div class="report-links">{{if .WatchURL}}<a href="{{.WatchURL}}">Watch recording ↗</a>{{end}}{{if .YouTube}}<a href="{{.YouTube}}">Watch on YouTube ↗</a>{{end}}{{if .X}}<a href="{{.X}}">Watch on X ↗</a>{{end}}</div>{{end}}
{{define "report_paper"}}
<div class="paper-edition">
<section class="paper-sheet paper-cover" aria-label="Report cover">
  <header class="paper-masthead"><span>bitcoin++</span><span>FIELD NOTES / 2026<br>PARTNER EDITION</span></header>
  <div class="paper-cover-title"><p class="paper-kicker">{{.Event.Period}} · {{.Event.Location}}</p><h1>{{if eq .Event.Tag "nairobi"}}Nairobi.<br><em>Built in<br>the open.</em>{{else}}{{.Event.Location}}<br><em>Built in the open.</em>{{end}}</h1></div>
  {{with .Event.LeadImage}}<figure class="paper-cover-art"><img src="{{.}}" alt="{{$.Event.Title}} event artwork"><figcaption>THE OPEN SOURCE EDITION / EVENT ARTWORK</figcaption></figure>{{end}}
  <div class="paper-cover-bottom"><div><p class="paper-kicker">A gathering. A body of work.</p><p>The people, ideas and projects<br>behind {{.Event.Title}}.</p></div><div><p class="paper-kicker">Prepared for</p>{{template "report_recipient_logo" .}}<p data-report-recipient>{{.PreparedFor}}</p></div></div>
  <footer class="paper-folio"><span>bitcoin++ / {{.Event.Tag}}</span><span>Event report · editorial draft</span></footer>
</section>

<section class="paper-sheet paper-opening" aria-label="Opening and event evidence">
  <div class="paper-running"><span>01 / A note from nifty</span><span>{{.Event.Location}}</span></div>
  <h2>A new place.<br><em>The same conviction.</em></h2>
  <div data-section="note" class="paper-letter"><div class="story-text report-markdown">{{(.Section "note").Markdown}}</div></div>
  {{with .HeadlineEvidence}}<div class="paper-facts" aria-label="Sourced event figures">{{range .}}<article><strong>{{.Value}}</strong><span>{{.Label}}</span></article>{{end}}</div>{{end}}
  <p class="paper-source">{{if .Preview}}Published program and project gallery · {{.EvidenceDate}}. Workshop delivery is not yet reviewed. Hackathon participants are distinct project members; their total requires connected event records. A dash means unavailable, not zero.{{else}}Event records · {{.Generated}}. Definitions and review notes at the end of this report.{{end}}</p>

  <footer class="paper-folio"><span>With thanks to <span data-report-recipient>{{.PreparedFor}}</span></span><span>People & purpose</span></footer>
</section>

<section id="participation" class="paper-sheet paper-participation" aria-label="Participation and program totals"><div class="paper-running"><span>The gathering in numbers</span><span>People · program · recordings</span></div><h2>The people.<br><em>The work they shared.</em></h2>
<div class="paper-facts">{{if .ShowRegistrations}}<article><strong>{{.Registrations}}</strong><span>registration records</span></article>{{end}}<article><strong>{{.SpeakerCount}}</strong><span>distinct program speakers</span></article><article><strong>{{.RecordingCount}}</strong><span>sessions with recording links</span></article></div>
<p class="paper-source">{{if .DemoAttendance}}SAMPLE DATA: registrations and unique check-ins come from the isolated local demo database, not Nairobi attendance. Production uses actual event records.{{else if .Preview}}Attendance and registration records are not connected to this public preview. They must be populated before this report is sponsor-ready.{{else}}Attendance is deduplicated from check-ins. Registrations are records, not a second attendance total.{{end}} Speaker totals include panelists and workshop presenters. Recording links indicate availability, not views.</p>
{{with .ProgramSummary}}{{template "paper_chart" .}}{{end}}
{{with .StageDemand}}{{template "report_stage_demand" .}}{{end}}
<p>Online audience figures have their own “Beyond the room” page. They measure the reach of recordings and posts separately from the people who attended.</p><footer class="paper-folio"><span>Scheduled does not mean delivery-confirmed</span><span>{{.EvidenceDate}}</span></footer></section>
{{range $sheet,$people := .SpeakerSheets}}
<section id="speaker-community-{{$sheet}}" class="paper-sheet paper-speaker-mosaic" aria-label="Full speaker community"><div class="paper-running"><span>The people behind the program</span><span>{{$.Event.Location}}</span></div><h2>Meet the builders.<br><em>Every voice in the room.</em></h2><div data-section="speakers_intro"><div class="story-text report-markdown paper-intro-small">{{($.Section "speakers_intro").Markdown}}</div></div><div class="speaker-mosaic">{{range .}}<figure>{{if .Photo}}<img src="{{.Photo}}" alt="{{.Name}}" loading="eager">{{else}}<div class="mosaic-no-photo" aria-label="Portrait unavailable">++</div>{{end}}<figcaption><strong>{{.Name}}</strong>{{with .Company}}<span>{{.}}</span>{{end}}</figcaption></figure>{{end}}</div><footer class="paper-folio"><span>Contributors · educators · application builders</span><span>bitcoin++</span></footer></section>
{{end}}
{{with .ProgramDays}}<section id="program-timeline" class="paper-sheet paper-timeline" aria-label="Three-day program timeline"><div class="paper-running"><span>The rhythm of the gathering</span><span>{{$.Event.Timezone}} · local time</span></div><h2>Three days.<br><em>Many conversations.</em></h2><div data-section="timeline_intro"><div class="story-text report-markdown paper-intro-small">{{($.Section "timeline_intro").Markdown}}</div></div><div class="timeline-key"><span>● Talks / keynotes</span><span>● Workshops</span><span>● Panels</span></div><div class="program-days">{{range .}}<section><h3>{{.Label}}</h3>{{range .Items}}<article class="program-slot program-slot--{{.Kind}}"><p>{{.Time}}{{with .Venue}} · {{.}}{{end}}</p>{{if .URL}}<a href="{{.URL}}">{{.Title}}</a>{{else}}<strong>{{.Title}}</strong>{{end}}</article>{{end}}</section>{{end}}</div><footer class="paper-folio"><span>Explore the full program at btcpp.dev/{{$.Event.Tag}}/agenda</span><span>Published schedule</span></footer></section>{{end}}
<section id="speaker-map" class="paper-sheet paper-geography" aria-label="Speaker geography"><div class="paper-running"><span>A global developer community</span><span>Speaker locations</span></div><h2>Many places.<br><em>One conversation.</em></h2><div data-section="geography_intro"><div class="story-text report-markdown">{{($.Section "geography_intro").Markdown}}</div></div>
<svg class="speaker-globes" viewBox="0 0 720 350" role="img" aria-label="Two globe hemispheres with resolved speaker origins"><image href="/static/img/report-globes.svg" width="720" height="350"/>{{range .MappedSpeakers}}<circle cx="{{.X}}" cy="{{.Y}}" r="5" fill="#f7b500" stroke="#242124"><title>{{.Name}} · {{.Place}}</title></circle>{{end}}</svg>
<p class="paper-source">{{len .ReportedSpeakerLocations}} of {{.SpeakerCount}} program speakers have reported origins; {{len .MappedSpeakers}} are mapped. Recognized cities use approximate centres from <a href="https://www.geonames.org/">GeoNames</a> (<a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>); unresolved origins are listed but not plotted. These are self-reported travel origins, not nationality or verified journeys.</p>
<div class="speaker-location-list">{{range .ReportedSpeakerLocations}}<p><strong>{{.Name}}</strong><br>{{.Place}}<br><small>{{.Source}}</small></p>{{else}}<p>Travel origins load automatically from speaker event forms in the connected admin report. This public preview does not contain those form responses. No locations have been guessed.</p>{{end}}</div>
<footer class="paper-folio"><span>Land outlines: Natural Earth · public domain</span><span>Geographic coverage, not attendance</span></footer></section>
<section class="paper-sheet" aria-label="Technical program">
  <div class="paper-running"><span>02 / The technical conversation</span><span>Open source, in practice</span></div>
  <h2>From using Bitcoin<br><em>to building it.</em></h2>
  <div data-section="program"><div class="story-text report-markdown paper-deck">{{(.Section "program").Markdown}}</div></div>
  <div class="paper-speakers">{{range .HighlightSpeakers}}<figure>{{if .Photo}}<img src="{{.Photo}}" alt="Portrait of {{.Name}}" loading="lazy">{{end}}<figcaption><strong>{{.Name}}</strong><span>{{.Company}}</span></figcaption></figure>{{end}}</div>
  <div data-section="panels"><div class="story-text report-markdown paper-source">{{(.Section "panels").Markdown}}</div></div>
  <div class="paper-discussions">{{range $i,$p := .Panels}}<article><span class="paper-index">0{{if eq $i 0}}1{{else if eq $i 1}}2{{else}}3{{end}}</span><div><h3>{{$p.Title}}</h3><p class="paper-byline">{{$p.Speakers}}</p>{{with $p.Note}}<p>{{.}}</p>{{end}}{{template "report_recordings" $p}}</div></article>{{end}}</div>
  {{with .ChartFor "program"}}{{template "paper_chart" .}}{{end}}
  <footer class="paper-folio"><span>Editorial highlights · not a popularity ranking</span><a href="https://btcpp.dev/{{.Event.Tag}}/agenda">Explore the program ↗</a></footer>
</section>

<section class="paper-sheet paper-builds" aria-label="Hackathon winning projects">
  <div class="paper-running"><span>03 / What got built</span><span>From an idea to a prototype</span></div>
  <h2>The winning projects.<br><em>Built to stand out.</em></h2>
  <div data-section="hackathon"><div class="story-text report-markdown paper-deck">{{(.Section "hackathon").Markdown}}</div></div>
  <div class="paper-winners">{{range $i,$w := .Winners}}<article class="paper-project {{if eq $i 0}}paper-project-lead{{end}}">
    {{if .Image}}<img src="{{.Image}}" alt="{{.Title}} project artwork" loading="lazy">{{end}}
    <div><p class="paper-kicker">{{.Awards}}</p>{{with .PrizeFigure}}<p class="report-prize-amount"><strong>{{.Value}}</strong> {{.Label}}</p>{{end}}<h3><a href="https://btcpp.dev/{{$.Event.Tag}}/hackathon/projects/{{.PublicID}}">{{.Title}}</a></h3><p>{{.Description}}</p>{{with .Significance}}<p class="paper-meaning">{{.}}</p>{{end}}{{template "report_winner_team" .}}<div class="report-links">{{if .Demo}}<a href="{{.Demo}}">Explore project ↗</a>{{end}}{{if .GitHub}}<a href="{{.GitHub}}">Source code ↗</a>{{end}}</div></div>
  </article>{{end}}</div>
  {{with .WinnerAwardTotal}}<p class="paper-source">{{.}} sats in published overall awards across the projects shown. Awarded amounts are not confirmation of payment.</p>{{end}}
  {{with .ChartFor "teams"}}{{template "paper_chart" .}}{{end}}
  <footer class="paper-folio"><span>Prototypes shown · subsequent adoption not measured</span><a href="https://btcpp.dev/{{.Event.Tag}}/hackathon">Published results ↗</a></footer>
</section>

<section class="paper-sheet paper-community" aria-label="Community and judges">
  <div class="paper-running"><span>04 / The people around the work</span><span>Experience, shared</span></div>
